      "text": [
        ": \"اُكْتُبْ لِلْآبِقِ فِي وَرَقَةٍ أَوْ فِي قِرْطَاسٍ: \"بِسْمِ اَللّٰهِ اَلرَّحْمٰنِ اَلرَّحِيمِ\" يَدُ فُلاَنٍ مَغْلُولَةٌ إِلَى عُنُقِهِ إِذَا أَخْرَجَهَا ۝ لَمْ يَكَدْ يَرٰاهٰا وَ مَنْ لَمْ يَجْعَلِ اَللّٰهُ لَهُ نُوراً فَمٰا لَهُ مِنْ نُورٍ ۝ ثُمَّ لُفَّهَا ثُمَّ اِجْعَلْهَا بَيْنَ عُودَيْنِ ثُمَّ أَلْقِهَا فِي كَوَّةِ بَيْتٍ مُظْلِمٍ فِي اَلْمَوْضِعِ اَلَّذِي كَانَ يَأْوِي فِيهِ \"."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.3544 - Abu Jameelah narrated from Abdullah ibn Abi Ya'fur, from Abu Abdullah (as):\n\"Write for the runaway slave on a piece of paper or parchment: 'In the Name of Allah (swt), the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful. The hand of [slave's name] is tied to his neck. If he extends it, he will hardly see it. And whomever Allah (swt) has not granted light, for him there is no light (Surah An-Nur 24:40).'\nThen wrap it, place it between two sticks, and throw it into a dark corner of the house where he used to stay.\""
        ]
      }
    },
